All clean — `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` pass with no issues.

**Delivered:**

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `configuration.go` | `Source`, `Config`, `Load` — implementation of the contract |
| `configuration_test.go` | 7 test functions covering defaults, port parsing/validation (incl. boundary, bad input, NumError preservation), name validation (ErrSyntax), debug (ParseBool variants), and combined loading |
| `cmd/configprint/main.go` | CLI that loads from `os.LookupEnv` and prints `port=<p> name=<n> debug=<d>` |

**Key design decisions:**
- Bad port → `*strconv.NumError` from `Atoi` (or synthetic `NumError` with `ErrRange` for out-of-range ints) — callers can `errors.As`/`errors.Is` as spec requires
- Empty `HELIOS_NAME` → `strconv.ErrSyntax` (identifiable via `errors.Is`)
- No third-party dependencies, pure stdlib
- All tests verify error types, not just error presence
